{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema\/Enumeration"],"generated":true,"title":"Events","anchor":"Events"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:6Events15DiscoveredEventV","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscoveredEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscoveredEvent"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"DiscoveredEvent.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent.swift#L48"},"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Events"}],"title":"DiscoveredEvent"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event type found in the running program: one declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", or one of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own events, with its schema."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/schema","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/type"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Events\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscoveredEvent"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every one the program links, from every module, so a store or a tracking plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be built from it with no list to keep: "},{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DatabaseStore(database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TrackingPlan()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each use it."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","DiscoveredEvent.all.map { $0.type.name }","\/\/ [\"ApplicationBackgrounded\", ..., \"SessionStarted\", \"signed_up\"]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" struct is discovered, wherever it is declared, unless it is generic or nested in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a generic type, as neither can hold the record "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" places in the binary; the macro notes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one where it is declared. One declared in an extension of a generic type doesn’t compile."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The library’s own events are discovered too: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ControlActivated"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Application"},{"type":"text","text":" events of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LifecycleTracking"},{"type":"text","text":", once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their modules are linked. An event that conforms to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by hand, without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", isn’t:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it beside the discovered ones, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredEvent.all.map(\\.type) + [Legacy.self]"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Limits","text":"Limits","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An object file in a static archive that nothing references brings no record into the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"program: the linker leaves it out. That happens with CocoaPods’ static libraries, a static","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"XCFramework, or a Bazel library with ","type":"text"},{"code":"alwayslink = False","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". SwiftPM, and Bazel’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"alwayslink = True","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", link every object file. Link such a library whole (","type":"text"},{"code":"-force_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Apple platforms, ","type":"text"},{"code":"--whole-archive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on Linux) to have its events found.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" holds the events of the images loaded when it is called: the program and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic libraries it links. A library opened later with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adds its events from then on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that loads or unloads while ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"},{"text":" is read is either read whole or left out of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that read. On Apple platforms one that dyld adds before the read starts is found; on Linux a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlclose"},{"text":" waits for the read, so the library is missed. The next read sees it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlclose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a library that declares events while the process runs. On Apple platforms","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dyld keeps it mapped and its events are still found. On Linux the loader unmaps it while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift runtime keeps its types registered, and the process can crash later. Keep plug-ins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"open, or open them with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RTLD_NODELETE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A module that declares events, linked into two images, lists each of its events twice, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores and plans refuse the duplicate. Link each such module into one image.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/event